  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no completed experiments, there is zero evidence about any design choice, so the priority is establishing a strong, interpretable reference point. config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, concat) uses the most established and standard components across every dimension: scgpt is the most widely validated RNA encoder, resnet50 is the canonical image backbone, avgpool is the simplest aggregation, and concat is the simplest fusion. This 'canonical' multimodal multiprofile configuration serves as the natural anchor for the study. From this single data point, subsequent experiments can isolate one variable at a time (e.g., swap scgpt→pca_n2000 to test RNA encoder impact, swap resnet50→imagenet_vit_l to test image encoder impact, swap concat→weighted to test fusion, or drop to rna_only/image_only to test whether multimodality adds value over single-modality baselines). Choosing a more complex or non-standard configuration first would conflate multiple untested choices and make it harder to attribute performance to specific design decisions under a limited budget."
}

